From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:19:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: The backlight PWM off after S3 with the
 panel off

On S3 resume with the display left to the OS (gfx_resume_init off),
gma_setup_panel() still runs and enables the PWM of the PCH at 50%,
while the panel stays unpowered until the OS lights it. Linux resumes
with the panel as it was before the sleep; with the panel off, i915
leaves the backlight alone, the PWM stays enabled, and every entry
into PC8 warns *PCH PWM1 enabled* (on the W541 of the port, every
20-30 s for as long as the screen stayed off after a resume, as soon
as the package could reach PC7).

In _WAK after S3, but under macOS (which keeps the firmware's PWM and
sets only its duty cycle), clear the enable bit of BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL1
when PCH_PP_CONTROL says the panel is not powered: the state the OS
finds after a VBIOS that does not run on resume. The frequency stays.
With gfx_resume_init on, the panel is powered and nothing changes.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init; the same
change made by hand after a resume: no warning in 90 s with the screen
off, and with the screen on again i915 enabled the PWM at its level.

Change-Id: Ica0e54bbab0d8eb25ba950f2a6e8882b8fe8787f
---
 .../lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl          |  7 +++-
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/pnlf.asl    | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
index fb20c1aa1b..f973f7d62d 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
@@ -13,7 +13,9 @@ Method(_WAK,1)
 	/*
 	 * The firmware sets the backlight PWM at the frequency of the panel and
 	 * at 50%, at boot and at every resume from S3 (gma_setup_panel()).
-	 * Linux and Windows set their own level again, macOS keeps that one:
+	 * Linux and Windows set their own level again when they light the
+	 * panel, and after S3 find the PWM off if the panel is not powered
+	 * (GFX0.BLOF); macOS keeps the firmware's level:
 	 * there, with PNLF (the panel as built-in display) the maximum of the
 	 * PWM as macOS takes it, after S4 as well, and after S3 the last level
 	 * that _BCM or the brightness keys set or _BQC read (BRLV).
@@ -25,6 +27,9 @@ Method(_WAK,1)
 		If (Arg0 == 3 && \_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BRVA) {
 			\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.XBCM (\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BRLV)
 		}
+	} ElseIf (Arg0 == 3) {
+		/* The PWM off when the panel was left unpowered (BLOF) */
+		\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BLOF ()
 	}
 
 #if CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM)
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/pnlf.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/pnlf.asl
index efe98a1914..a834df3ce1 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/pnlf.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/pnlf.asl
@@ -14,6 +14,40 @@ External (\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.MPBI, IntObj)
 
 Scope (\_SB.PCI0.GFX0)
 {
+	/*
+	 * After S3 with the display left to the OS (gfx_resume_init off), the
+	 * panel is not powered (PCH_PP_CONTROL bit 0 clear), but the panel
+	 * setup of coreboot (gma_setup_panel()) enabled the PWM of the PCH at
+	 * 50%. An OS that resumes with the panel off does not touch it, and
+	 * i915 then finds it enabled at every entry into PC8 (*PCH PWM1
+	 * enabled*). Turn the PWM off, as the OS found it after a VBIOS that
+	 * does not run on resume; the OS enables it when it lights the panel.
+	 * The frequency (BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL2) stays.
+	 */
+	Method (BLOF, 0, Serialized)
+	{
+		Local0 = GMMB ()
+		If (Local0 != 0) {
+			OperationRegion (PPCR, SystemMemory, Local0 + 0xc7204, 4)
+			Field (PPCR, DWordAcc, NoLock, Preserve)
+			{
+				PPCT, 32,	/* PCH_PP_CONTROL */
+			}
+			OperationRegion (BLCR, SystemMemory, Local0 + 0xc8250, 4)
+			Field (BLCR, DWordAcc, NoLock, Preserve)
+			{
+				BLC1, 32,	/* BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL1 */
+			}
+			Local1 = PPCT
+			Local2 = BLC1
+			/* All ones: the GPU does not decode its MMIO, leave it */
+			If (Local1 != 0xffffffff && (Local1 & 1) == 0 &&
+			    (Local2 & 0x80000000)) {
+				BLC1 = Local2 & 0x7fffffff
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* 1 under macOS with the panel as built-in display */
 	Method (DWBI)
 	{
-- 
2.56.0

